1
00:00:23,450 --> 00:00:28,500
The desires of this world will fade away,

2
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:33,450
and you will be alone inside the grave…

3
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:39,190
The first question in the grave will come,

4
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:44,530
"Did you pray?" your Lord will ask!

5
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:50,080
The desires of this world will fade away,

6
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:54,990
and you will be alone inside the grave…

7
00:00:55,610 --> 00:01:00,540
Five times a day, from the mosque,

8
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:06,600
when you hear the call "Allahu Akbar",

9
00:01:06,640 --> 00:01:10,950
do not lie there in laziness,

10
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:16,480
life will run out — do not forget!

11
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:21,670
It is a virtue that washes sins away,

12
00:01:21,920 --> 00:01:27,110
it is a duty owed to the Creator…

13
00:01:27,390 --> 00:01:32,620
To heal the pains of the heart,

14
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:37,990
there is no medicine greater than sujood, my friend!

15
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:43,170
The desires of this world will fade away,

16
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:48,290
and you will be alone inside the grave…

17
00:01:48,790 --> 00:01:53,900
The first question in the grave will come,

18
00:01:54,180 --> 00:01:58,790
"Did you pray?" your Lord will ask!

19
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:04,440
Those who gave up prayer —

20
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:10,080
have they not thrown themselves into the fire of Hell…

21
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:15,230
On the Day to come, at the time of reckoning,

22
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:20,530
what use is shedding tears then?

23
00:02:20,740 --> 00:02:25,630
In the Lord's court, what will you say?

24
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:31,260
Will standing there empty-handed save you?

25
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:36,550
When the soul reaches the throat,

26
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:41,890
what use is weeping in regret?

27
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:47,170
The desires of this world will fade away,

28
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:52,190
and you will be alone inside the grave…

29
00:02:52,770 --> 00:02:57,920
The first question in the grave will come,

30
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:02,730
"Did you pray?" your Lord will ask!

31
00:03:03,290 --> 00:03:08,300
In the purity of wudu, spreading out the prayer mat,

32
00:03:08,790 --> 00:03:14,220
as you stand before your Master…

33
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:18,970
filling the heart with flowers of humility,

34
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:24,090
performing the prayer with khushu’ (a humble, focused heart)…

35
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:30,180
in supplications mixed with tears,

36
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:35,210
seek the mercy of your Lord…

37
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:40,470
The hope of the flower-garden of Paradise

38
00:03:40,780 --> 00:03:46,010
is the prayer — do not forget it…

39
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:51,220
If you stay firm on the path of prayer,

40
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:56,550
you will attain success in both worlds…

41
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:59,680
O my Lord… O my Lord…

42
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,180
O my Lord… O my Lord…

43
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:07,190
Lay your forehead down in sujood…

44
00:04:07,420 --> 00:04:12,570
seek the mercy of your Lord…

45
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:17,440
The desires of this world will fade away,

46
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:22,730
and you will be alone inside the grave…

47
00:04:23,450 --> 00:04:28,360
The first question in the grave will come,

48
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:33,430
"Did you pray?" your Lord will ask!

49
00:04:34,130 --> 00:04:38,780
The desires of this world will fade away,

50
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:44,070
and you will be alone inside the grave…

51
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:49,850
The first question in the grave will come,

52
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:54,380
"Did you pray?" your Lord will ask!

53
00:04:55,500 --> 00:05:00,700
If you stay firm on the path of prayer,

54
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:05,950
you will attain success in both worlds…

55
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:10,790
O my Lord… O my Lord…
